# DPorts Generator (shell)

The shell scripts in this directory generate a DPorts tree by merging the
FreeBSD Ports Collection with the overlays in this repository. They are the
earlier generation of the tooling and remain here as the ports-side scripts.

## Where the Python toolchain went

The `dportsv3` Python package that used to live in this directory — the
compose pipeline, the `overlay.dops` DSL and its engine, the migration
program, the build tracker, the chroot dev-env manager and the agentic
build-failure repair loop — now lives in its own repository, **Polytropos**.

It was moved out because it had grown into a substantial piece of software in
its own right, with its own release cycle, test suite and issue tracker, while
this repository is a data repository: ports overlays and patches.

Polytropos reads this repository as an input. Point it at a checkout with
`--delta-root`, or set `$DPORTS_DELTA_ROOT`.

## What remains here

| Script | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `merge.sh`, `merge-mk.sh` | merge FreeBSD ports with the DeltaPorts overlay |
| `bulk_dports.sh`, `true_bulk_list.sh`, `ramo_*.sh` | bulk build list generation |
| `dportsd`, `dports-daemon.sh` | the generator daemon |
| `quicksync.sh`, `sync1.sh` | sync helpers |
| `prune.sh`, `mask_NO_PACKAGE.sh` | tree maintenance |
| `report_unbuilt.sh`, `never_tried.sh`, `stinkers.sh` | build reporting |
| `generate_ports_INDEX.sh`, `category-makefiles.sh` | index and category Makefiles |
| `rollingUPDATING.sh` | UPDATING entries |
| `identify-custom-nobody.sh` | audit helper |

`dports-default.conf` and `dports.toml.example` configure these scripts.

See also `scripts/new-generator/`, a filter-phase based rewrite of `merge.sh`.
